    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** headlining the daily projections. Boasting a 74.39 efficiency score, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** faces a favorable matchup against Fisher, where a combination of a +14% platoon edge and a +9% SP skill boost makes him our primary anchor. **Drake Baldwin** follows closely at 69.55, capitalizing on a weak 4.71 xERA starter and a strong #2 spot in the lineup. While **Heliot Ramos** (62.74) offers a solid floor, the most intriguing value lies in **Wade Meckler** (59.97); despite a modest base projection, his lead-off role combined with a +19% matchup against Dobnak makes him an essential start, especially given our focus on his potential for stolen bases against a targetable pitcher.\n\nRegarding bench decisions, **Sam Antonacci** narrowly secured the final infield spot over the field, largely due to the tactical advantage of his leadoff position (+10%) and a positive platoon split. **Miguel Vargas** remains the most significant bench/utility consideration; he carries a respectable 52.78 score and strong xwOBA indicators, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench in favor of hitters with more favorable volume-based scoring environments. We must keep a close eye on **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; both are struggling with sub-45 scores today as they contend with Seymour, who brings a daunting 3.34 xERA and creates a difficult path to efficiency for our left-handed bats.\n\nRisk mitigation is paramount today as we navigate a few concerning variables. We are actively monitoring the injury statuses of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined, alongside **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, who are currently out of their respective lineups. Additionally, while **Andy Pages** benefits from wind-assisted power potential, he faces a stiff test against Misiorowski, who boasts the lowest xERA (2.03) of any pitcher on our opposing slate. We will continue to lean on the stolen base upside of players like **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** to bolster our 5x5 totals, though we are wary of **Nasim Nunez** facing a pitcher who effectively limits the running game.",
